@startuml
title Approve a privileged action

actor Owner
participant "Agent session" as Agent
participant "PreToolUse hook" as Hook
database Ledger
participant "avarice approve" as Approve

note over Agent, Hook : two callers reach the hook with a shell command:\na unit of a run (scope is the run), or the owner's own\nhost session with the attended hook installed (scope is that session)

== A line with privileged commands is refused ==
Agent -> Hook : shell line, possibly with several commands
Hook -> Hook : classify every command of the line (push, pull request create, merge or edit,\nrelease create, API write, package publish)
alt no privileged command
  Hook --> Agent : this check says nothing; a run's command rules,\nor in an attended session the host's own rules, decide
else the line cannot be read, in a run
  Hook --> Agent : denied as a shell syntax error, no request
else a privileged command, in a run
  Hook -> Ledger : request for the first privileged command's scope, action and parameter digest\n(the waiting one again, else a new one), and the denial
  Hook --> Agent : denied, the owner approves with: avarice approve REQUEST
else attended session
  alt the line cannot be read
    Hook -> Ledger : the denial, no request
    Hook --> Agent : denied as unparseable, split the line or use the Write tool
  else a command takes its body from a file or standard input
    Hook -> Ledger : one denial for each such command, no request
    Hook --> Agent : denied as unapprovable, pass the fields inline
  else every privileged command is bound to its parameters, the exact line and the directory
    Hook -> Ledger : take one usable approval for each command (scope, action, digest), oldest first
    alt every command has an approval
      Ledger --> Hook : all approvals consumed, one action start for each, one transaction
      Hook --> Agent : no output, the line goes on to the host's own rules
    else one or more commands have none
      Ledger --> Hook : nothing consumed, the partial take is rolled back
      Hook -> Ledger : a request for each command without an approval\n(the waiting one again, else a new one), and a denial for each
      Hook --> Agent : denied, one avarice approve REQUEST clause for each missing approval
    end
  end
end
note over Hook : a run never consumes an approval: the denial stands\nwhether or not one was granted

== The owner approves ==
Owner -> Approve : approve REQUEST
alt not a terminal, inside a run, from a run's process tree,\nor not the user who owns the profile
  Approve --> Owner : refused (64), nothing written
else request unknown
  Approve --> Owner : refused (64)
else request already approved
  Approve --> Owner : not applied (3)
else request found
  Approve --> Owner : action, scope, parameter summary, digest,\nand "one use, 30 minutes"
  Owner --> Approve : yes or no
  alt anything but yes
    Approve --> Owner : not approved (0), nothing written
  else yes
    Approve -> Ledger : approval for exactly these parameters, granted by the owner
    Approve --> Owner : granted, used once, expires in 30 minutes (0)
  end
end

== The owner takes an approval back ==
Owner -> Approve : approve --revoke APPROVAL
alt approval unknown
  Approve --> Owner : refused (64)
else already revoked or already consumed
  Approve --> Owner : not applied (3)
else usable
  Approve -> Ledger : approval revoked
  Approve --> Owner : revoked (0)
end

== The retry ==
Agent -> Hook : the same line, same session, same directory
alt attended session, an approval unexpired and unused for each privileged command
  Hook -> Ledger : approvals consumed with the actions' starts
  Hook --> Agent : the line passes once
else run, or an approval expired, revoked, used or for other parameters,\na changed line or another directory
  Hook -> Ledger : a new request, since the earlier one was answered
  Hook --> Agent : denied again, with the new request
end
@enduml
